& [PreparedRuntimeCandidate] is not yet implementation authority
  + [candidate] is cache an immutable fabric bound to the exact environment digest and admitted package set
  + [candidate] is preserve cheap per-request envelope, scope, expected-set, budget, and response-proof validation
  + [invalidation] is any environment, trust-store, time, revocation, package, compiler-policy, or protocol-policy change
  + [proof_gate] is exact ProtocolResponse equivalence for success, partial, trust, policy, budget, ambiguity, and inspect outcomes
  + [concurrency_gate] is immutable thread-safe reads and bounded memory
  + [security_gate] is no stale admission, bootstrap weakening, caller self-authorization, or proof omission
  + [activation] is a separately source-preserved and SJS-processed slice rather than an implicit Phase6 database change

& [OwnershipAndMemoryBoundary] is unresolved before activation
  + [current_environment] owns every CompiledSourcePackage
  + [current_admission] clones the complete CompiledSourcePackage into AdmittedPackage
  + [current_fabric] additionally clones semantic units, relations, labels, and identities into query indexes
  + [naive_cache_risk] is retaining both EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment and SemanticFabric duplicates package content and adds index copies for the resident lifetime
  + [candidate_ownership] is share immutable packages through explicit ownership or let PreparedRuntime replace rather than duplicate the raw environment after preserving digest, trust, time, and expected-package proof inputs
  + [memory_gate] is measured peak and retained heap at representative source, unit, relation, quote, and label shapes
  - never: infer heap cost from serialized JSON bytes alone

& [ReadConcurrencyProbe] is candidate evidence rather than protocol proof
  + [compile_property] is SemanticFabric is Send and Sync
  + [probe] is eight threads each execute sixteen queries against one immutable Arc SemanticFabric
  + [scale] is 32 signed packages
  + [result] is 128 prepared query results exactly equal each other and the query result inside the full ProtocolResponse
  + [limitation] is no concurrent preparation, invalidation, environment swap, protocol-envelope execution, memory, latency, or service-load claim
